{
  "about": "What Flint writes the harness's texts from (agent.py texts): every system prompt, tool and parameter description, task statement template, change note and tool message a session can contain. Each request is a short instruction plus the facts as JSON with plain-word keys: names, parameters, limits, placeholders and values of at most four words, so the request holds no wording to copy. A text passes only if it shares no run of 5 words with any text this pipeline's authors wrote (these instructions and facts, texts_spec_v1.json, the tool runner's default messages), holds no underscore name that is not one of its facts' identifiers, does not describe its own format or name its tone or length, follows a 'wrapped in' format, Flint judges it consistent with its facts and natural, and its placeholders, length and the held-out rule check out; a text that fails only by copying is reworded by Flint. Requests are configuration and never enter a dataset; what enters is Flint's reply, recorded in texts.json with its seed and the hash of the generated tokens.",
  "version": 2,
  "instructions": {
    "system": "Below, as JSON, are the facts of the setting an autonomous coding agent works in. Write the system prompt the agent receives before each task: say what it has and cannot do, and add the working habits you think a careful agent should keep. Address the agent as \"you\", 60 to 180 words, plain text without headings or lists. Write natural sentences in your own words; do not repeat the JSON's keys. Output only the prompt.",
    "tool": "Below, as JSON, is a tool a coding agent can call. Write the tool's description field: one or two sentences, at most 30 words, on what it does and its limits. Write natural sentences in your own words, not the JSON's keys; tool and parameter names are fine. Output only the description.",
    "param": "Below, as JSON, is one parameter of a tool a coding agent can call. Write the parameter's description: a plain English phrase of at most 15 words that says what the agent passes in it. Output only the description.",
    "template": "Below, as JSON, is a coding task. Write the message in which a developer asks a coding agent to do it. The tone and length say how to write it; do not mention them. Each value in curly braces, such as {name}, is a placeholder: put each one in the message exactly once, with its braces. Write natural sentences in your own words; do not repeat the JSON's keys. Output only the message.",
    "note": "Below, as JSON, is a fact about a source file. Write one sentence of at most 25 words for a comment at the top of that file, stating the fact. Each value in curly braces is a placeholder: put each one in the sentence exactly once, with its braces. Use your own words. Output only the sentence.",
    "message": "Below, as JSON, is a message a coding agent's tool returns. Write the message as one short line of at most 20 words. Each value in curly braces is a placeholder: put each one in the line exactly once, with its braces; if the JSON has none, the line has no curly braces at all. If the JSON gives characters the line is wrapped in, the line starts and ends with them; do not describe them. Use your own words. Output only the line.",
    "judge": "Below are facts as JSON and a text written from them. Answer YES only if the text states something a fact contradicts, leaves out a fact listed under must mention, or is clumsy or ungrammatical English; otherwise answer NO. The text may leave out every other fact, and it may say the facts in its own words: a fact said differently is still kept. Names of tools and parameters (such as read_file or old_string) and values in curly braces may appear in the text but are not required. Put YES or NO on the first line, then the reason in one line.",
    "rephrase": "Reword the text below so that it says the same thing in different words. Keep each value in curly braces exactly as it is. Output only the new text."
  },
  "variants": {"system": 3, "system_pi": 2, "write_tests": 4, "fix_bug": 6, "implement": 4, "change_note": 1},
  "tones": ["terse", "friendly", "issue-tracker ticket", "casual chat", "formal", "slightly impatient"],
  "lengths": ["one sentence", "two or three sentences", "a short paragraph"],
  "system": {
    "agx": {"role": "autonomous coding agent", "project folder": "/work", "tools": ["list_dir", "read_file", "search", "edit_file", "write_file", "run_tests", "run_command"], "internet access": "none", "can install software": "no", "tasks come from": "a developer", "must mention": ["project folder", "internet access", "can install software"]},
    "pi": {"role": "autonomous coding agent", "project folder": "/work", "tools": ["read", "write", "edit", "bash"], "tests are run with": "bash", "internet access": "none", "can install software": "no", "tasks come from": "a developer", "must mention": ["project folder", "internet access", "can install software", "tests are run with"]}
  },
